hes).\nThis is preventing caches from establishing themselves, driving up costs for recompiles.\n\nI'm not sure if you can access my build logs, but you can see the fail on all systems:\nhttps://github.com/Ivorforce/godot/actions/runs/14173236379/job/39701883100\n\nThe reason seems to be that `CACHE_TIMESTAMP` is missing:\n```bash\nmisc/scripts/purge_cache.py  \"/home/runner/work/godot/godot/.scons_cache/\"\nusage: purge_cache.py [-h] timestamp directory\npurge_cache.py: error: argument timestamp: invalid int value: '/home/runner/work/godot/godot/.scons_cache/'\n```\n\nWhich in turn probably happens because the restore failed:\n```\nCache not found for input keys: linux-template-mono|master|0ba487978671e046b63821dc0afb129f3e4b667a, linux-template-mono|master\nRun test -d \"/home/runner/work/godot/godot/.scons_cache/\" && find \"/home/runner/work/godot/godot/.scons_cache/\" >> redundant.txt\nError: Process completed with exit code 1.\n```\n\nSo, if I'm understanding correctly, it's failing to save because there's no cache to restore, and there's no cache to restore because it's failing to save 😅\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Make a fork\n- Push a commit to trigger CI\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A\n\ncc @Repiteo ","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"http